{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>That which came to his hand.</b> In his possession — and likewise ״וַיִּקַּח אֶת כָּל אַרְצוֹ מִיָּדוֹ״ (Numbers 21). And others say: from that which came to his hand — precious stones and pearls, which a person binds up in a bundle and carries in his hand. Others say: from that which came to his hand — from the unconsecrated property, from which he took tithe, as you say ״עַשֵּׂר אֲעַשְּׂרֶנּוּ לָךְ״, and afterwards took a gift."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "דָּ״אַ (דבר אחר) rendered 'others say' following Rashi's standard marker for an additional interpretation."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:43.928582114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}